julie (solutions-eng): Hey team — we're trialing Bugsnag for the web app next week. Quick security/privacy check: our SPA currently sends error.message, stack, user.id, user.email, and a few request headers. Do we need to strip/hash anything before sending to a third-party error tracker?

kevin (backend): sample payload we send now: ```{
  "error": "TypeError: x is undefined",
  "user": {"id": "user_12345", "email": "mike@example.com"},
  "path": "/checkout"
}``` Can we just hash user.id and drop email?

sam (eng-security): Short answer: yes. No plaintext emails, SSNs, CC numbers in vendor logs. Requirements: field-level redaction or hashing (user ids ok if hashed with a salt), retention <= 90d unless vendor has a DPA with stricter limits, and SSO + SCIM or tightly-scoped API keys for account access. Also ensure role-based access for the project.

maria (privacy): Also add DPA review + confirm EU residency for any EU user data. If you plan to send email hashes, document the hashing algorithm and salt management. Please fill our vendor questionnaire: https://go.redwood/vendor-questionnaire and attach it to the JIRA.

anthony (devex): For browser-side redaction we typically do this pattern: ```js
Bugsnag.start({
  releaseStage: 'production',
  user: { id: hash(user.id) }, // hash on client or strip and add server-provided token
  onError: (event) => {
    // scrub anything that looks like an email or cc in metadata
    delete event.__payload?.request?.body;
  }
});
``` We can keep stack traces but scrub any path/query params containing emails.

ops-bot: Access request created: VENDOR-322 assigned to @sam. Approvers requested: @maria, @julie. Jira: https://jira.redwood/browse/VENDOR-322

julie (solutions-eng): Thanks. I'll scope the frontend to only send hashed user id + anonymous session, no email. Kevin — can you add server middleware to strip headers (authorization, cookie) and hash ids on the backend before forwarding to Bugsnag?

kevin (backend): Yep — I'll add a middleware patch, send a PR, and link to VENDOR-322. ETA EOD today. Will also include unit tests for redaction.

sam (eng-security): One more note: do not enable session replay or network capture features. If you need request bodies for debugging, route them to an internal sink or use the private deployment option.

julie (solutions-eng): :thumbsup: Sounds good. I'll update the runbook and attach the vendor questionnaire to the ticket.

kevin (backend): PR open: https://github.com/redwood-inference/webapp/pull/459 — added hash + header strip. tagging @julie @sam for review.

maria (privacy): I'll do the DPA check once the questionnaire is in. If vendor can't guarantee EU residency, we need a mitigation plan.

anthony (devex): If anyone wants a pre-approved template, we have a Bugsnag config snippet in the docs repo (docs/tools/err-tracking.md). Happy to link it in the PR.

julie (solutions-eng): great — closing the loop here. If anything changes, thread in VENDOR-322. Thanks everyone.
